export const constants = {"MISSING_RESULT_POLICY":"MISSING RESULTS POLICY: Every approved, applicable required criterion must be checked. When the entire target source has been read clearly and a required field/result/attachment is genuinely absent or its cell is explicitly blank, return presence=\"missing\", value=\"누락\", uncertain=false, status=\"fail\". An absence is a failure of the requirement, not a numeric zero. Cite the actual same-row identifier or relevant table/section that was inspected; never invent a quote saying a value is missing. Distinguish absence from inability to read: obscured/cropped/low-quality text, missing source pages, unprocessed ranges, extraction limits, missing formula caches or uncertain applicability require presence=\"unreadable\" or \"unknown\", uncertain=true, status=\"review\". Do not infer absence merely because an extraction omitted a field. ND, N/A and printed dashes are source notations, not proof of absence. Optional fields do not fail when absent; do not emit out-of-scope criteria. A normal readable value uses presence=\"present\". These handling rules take precedence over older generic suggestions to send every blank to human review.","CRITERIA_NOTES_POLICY":"CRITERIA NOTES POLICY: The user excludes ALL content of source columns/fields explicitly headed 비고, 참고, Note(s), or Remark(s). Never use those cells for a requirement, prerequisite, scope, category, matching constraint, warning, or verdict, including ages such as 28일, temperatures, exceptions, aliases, and qualitative obligations. Original documents may still display these cells for reference. Preserve conditions actually stated in criterion/item/type/test-condition columns, outside the excluded fields, or explicitly requested by the user in natural language. Do not globally remove ages or conditions by wording alone. This policy applies to spreadsheets, CSV, PDF/Word tables and transposed tables alike.","MAX_FIELDS":300,"MAX_ROUNDS":3};
