const DOCUMENT_UNIT_POLICY=`Separate faithful source-structure interpretation from business-policy requirements. A unit column may correctly be blank for a qualitative, boolean, categorical or textual criterion such as a condition/state requirement. Do not invent a physical unit, ask whether that normal blank was intentional, or mark the region uncertain solely because a nonnumeric criterion has no unit. Preserve the blank as printed and, if useful, describe it as unit not applicable. Conversely, preserve a real ambiguity when a numeric measurement needs a missing unit, ND/detection-limit notation is unclear, the unit/header association is uncertain, source-required metadata is missing, or a unit actually present in the source was omitted or misread. A qualitative criterion never authorizes ignoring numeric-unit problems elsewhere in the same document.`;
